---
import LegalPage, { type LegalSection } from '../components/site/LegalPage.astro';
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../data/site';
import { CONSENT_KEY } from '../lib/consent';

const mailto = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;

const sections: LegalSection[] = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are and what this covers', toc: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'information-we-collect', title: 'Information we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', title: 'How we use information', toc: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'legal-bases', title: 'Legal bases' },
  { id: 'sharing', title: 'Who we share information with', toc: 'Sharing' },
  { id: 'international-transfers', title: 'International transfers' },
  { id: 'retention', title: 'How long we keep information', toc: 'Retention' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Security' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy', toc: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact us', toc: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  muted="In plain words."
  description="How Aldente AI handles personal information on aldenteai.com and in Aldo, Aldente Verify and Aldente Vision, and the rights you have."
  lead="What we collect, why we collect it, and the choices you have."
  updated="2026-10-06"
  sections={sections}
>
  <Fragment slot="summary">
    <ul>
      <li>Our website sets no cookies of its own. It only remembers your cookie choice, in your browser.</li>
      <li>We count visits with Plausible Analytics, which uses no cookies and collects no personal data.</li>
      <li>We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context advertising.</li>
      <li>When a business uses Aldo, Aldente Verify or Aldente Vision, we handle its data for it, under its agreement with us.</li>
      <li>To ask about your data, write to <a href={mailto}>{SITE.email}</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="who-we-are">
    <p>Aldente AI (“Aldente”, “we”, “us”) runs aldenteai.com and makes Aldo, Aldente Verify and Aldente Vision.</p>
    <p>
      This policy explains what personal information we collect when you visit this website, book a call with us or email us, and what
      we do with it. For that information, Aldente is the controller: we decide how it is used.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also explains our role when businesses use our products. For the data a business connects, that business is the controller
      and Aldente is its processor, or “service provider”. See <a href="#customer-data">when a business uses our products</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="information-we-collect">
    <h3>When you visit this website</h3>
    <p>
      We count visits with Plausible Analytics. It sets no cookies and collects no personal data. We see totals only: the pages
      viewed, the site that sent you, your browser, device type and country. Your IP address is not stored.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site remembers your cookie choice in your browser’s local storage, under the name “{CONSENT_KEY}”, for 12 months. It stays
      in your browser. Our <a href={LINKS.cookies}>cookie policy</a> has the details.
    </p>
    <p>
      Like any website, the servers that host it receive the technical details your browser sends with each request, such as your IP
      address, so they can deliver the pages.
    </p>

    <h3>When you book a call</h3>
    <p>
      The demo page uses Calendly to book calls. When you book, Calendly collects your name, email address, time zone and any answers
      you give, and passes them to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      Calendly asks for its own cookie consent on the demo page, unless you have accepted marketing cookies on this site, and sets its
      own cookies under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h3>When you email us</h3>
    <p>When you write to <a href={mailto}>{SITE.email}</a>, we receive your email address, your message and anything else you include.</p>

    <h3 id="customer-data">When a business uses our products</h3>
    <p>
      Aldo, Aldente Verify and Aldente Vision work with data that our business customers connect: camera footage, order and POS
      records, staff and schedule records, and messages in Slack, Telegram or WhatsApp. This can include information about staff and
      guests.
    </p>
    <p>
      We process this data for the customer, on its instructions and under its agreement with us. The customer is the controller and
      decides why and how the data is used. Aldente is its processor, or “service provider”.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you work at or visit one of our customers and have a question about your data, please contact that business first. If you
      write to us, we will pass your request to the business and help it respond.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="how-we-use-it">
    <p>We use personal information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>run, secure and improve this website, using the totals from Plausible</li>
      <li>arrange the calls you book, hold them and follow up afterwards</li>
      <li>answer your emails and questions</li>
      <li>provide Aldo, Aldente Verify and Aldente Vision to our customers, as their agreements set out</li>
      <li>meet our legal obligations and protect our rights</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We use customer data in our products only as the customer’s agreement allows.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="legal-bases">
    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, the GDPR and UK GDPR require a legal basis for each use of your
      personal information. We rely on these:
    </p>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Contract</dt>
        <dd>To take the steps you ask for before a contract, such as booking a call, and to provide our services to customers.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Legitimate interests</dt>
        <dd>
          To run, secure and improve our website, to answer questions, and to follow up with businesses interested in our products. We
          rely on this only when your rights do not outweigh these interests.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Consent</dt>
        <dd>
          Where we ask for it, such as for marketing cookies. You can withdraw it at any time in{' '}
          <button type="button" data-cookie-settings>cookie settings</button>.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Legal obligation</dt>
        <dd>When the law requires us to keep or share information.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>For customer data in our products, the customer decides the legal basis, as the controller.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sharing">
    <p>We share personal information only with service providers that process it for us, under contract:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Calendly</strong>, to book calls.</li>
      <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong>, to count visits. It stores no personal data.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure providers</strong> that run our website and services.</li>
      <li><strong>Email and business software</strong> we use to run the company and answer you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also share information when the law requires it, to protect our rights or the safety of others, or if Aldente is part of a
      merger, acquisition or sale of assets. In that case your information stays protected by this policy.
    </p>
    <p>Customer data in our products is shared only as the customer’s agreement allows.</p>
    <p><strong>We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.</strong></p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="international-transfers">
    <p>
      Our service providers may process information in countries other than the one where you live, including outside the European
      Economic Area and the United Kingdom. Those countries may have different data protection laws.
    </p>
    <p>When we transfer personal information across borders, we use the safeguards the law requires.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="retention">
    <p>We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes in this policy, or as long as the law requires.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your cookie choice:</strong> 12 months in your browser, then we ask again.</li>
      <li><strong>Visit statistics:</strong> Plausible keeps totals only, with no personal data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bookings and emails:</strong> while we are in touch with you, and for a reasonable time afterwards. You can ask us to delete
        them sooner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Customer data:</strong> for the period set in the customer’s agreement. Customers can set how long footage and records are
        kept, per location.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="security">
    <p>
      We protect personal information with technical and organisational measures suited to the risk. Our{' '}
      <a href={LINKS.security}>Security page</a> explains how we protect customer data.
    </p>
    <p>If you think something is wrong, tell us at <a href={mailto}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="your-rights">
    <p>Depending on where you live, you can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>give you a copy of your personal information (access)</li>
      <li>correct it if it is wrong</li>
      <li>delete it</li>
      <li>stop using it for some purposes (objection)</li>
      <li>limit how we use it (restriction)</li>
      <li>send it to you or to another company in a common format (portability)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Where we rely on your consent, you can withdraw it at any time. This does not affect what we did before.</p>
    <p>
      To use any of these rights, write to <a href={mailto}>{SITE.email}</a>. We may need to confirm who you are first. We reply within the
      time the law sets, and we will not treat you differently for using your rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority, for example where you live or work. We would welcome the chance
      to help first.
    </p>

    <h3>If you live in California</h3>
    <p>
      California law gives you the right to know what personal information we collect and how we use and share it, and to ask us to
      delete or correct it. You can also opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal information. We do not sell it or share it for
      cross-context behavioural advertising, so there is nothing to opt out of. You can make a request through an authorised agent, and
      we will not discriminate against you for using your rights.
    </p>

    <h3>If your data is in our products</h3>
    <p>If your information is in one of our customers’ workspaces, that business handles your request, and we help it respond.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="children">
    <p>
      This website is for businesses. It is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their personal
      information. If you believe a child has given us personal information, write to us and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="changes">
    <p>
      We update this policy when our practices or the law change. The date at the top of this page shows the latest version. If we make
      a significant change, we will say so here.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="contact">
    <p>
      For questions or requests about privacy, write to Aldente AI at <a href={mailto}>{SITE.email}</a> or call{' '}
      <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class="nowrap">{SITE.phone}</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</LegalPage>
